# Dataset blobs: never apply text or end-of-line conversion.
#
# This is not theoretical. flow.bin encodes each velocity component as
# sign(c)*sqrt(|c|/scale)*127 + 128, so every byte lands in 1..255 and the file
# contains no NUL at all. Git's content heuristic only looks for a NUL in the
# first 8000 bytes, so it classifies flow.bin as TEXT -- it shows up in
# `git show --stat` as "1 +" rather than "Bin". Today the byte values that would
# matter (0x0A) happen not to occur, but the mapping depends on the per-dataset
# `scale`, so a regenerated file can contain them. With core.autocrlf=true, a
# checkout would then expand each 0x0A to 0x0D0A and shift the whole field --
# a corrupted flow layer with no error anywhere.
*.bin binary
*.nc  binary

# Keep the obvious ones explicit too, so nothing depends on content sniffing.
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
